    "result_text": "Done. Version 2 of the owner identity is implemented and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What changed\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in, so every identifier changes and no V1 value recurs)**\n- New `util/IdentityVersion.java` \u2014 single source for `TAG = \"V2\"`, `API_VERSION = 2`, `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`.\n- `AssignMemberId` \u2014 the `REGION` component inside `memberId` is now the plain region **plus** the `V2` tag (e.g. `NSWV2273F1A9C2B4`).\n- `Household` \u2014 `householdId` is now SHA-256 over `lastName | postcode | V2`.\n- `OwnerIdentityKey` \u2014 `identityKey` is now SHA-256 over `telephone | email | soundex(lastName) | V2`.\n\n**`locality` stays the plain region (not an identifier)**\n- `OwnerMapper` no longer reads the region back off the (now V2-tagged) `memberId`. `locality`, `timezone`, and the `ownerSegment` region are recomputed straight from postcode/city via `LocalityResolver.localityOf(postcode, city)` \u2014 yielding the same plain `NSW`, with no `V2` tag leaking in.\n\n**Response shape**\n- `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` moved out of the top level into a nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema in `openapi.yml`, generated as `OwnerIdentityDto`, populated by a mapper helper).\n- New top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n\n**Audit schema**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON now leads with `\"schemaVersion\":2`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. Verified in the run: `AUDIT - {\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",...}` and the acceptance test's structural contract (`$.apiVersion == 2`, nested `identity.*` present, top-level `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` absent) passes.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the exact placement of the `V2` tag within each identifier (region-suffix in `memberId`, appended hash input for `householdId`/`identityKey`) is my faithful reading of the spec \u2014 the spec fixes the tag value and the resulting shape (nested `identity`, `apiVersion`/`schemaVersion` = 2) but not the precise byte-level mixing, and only the structural contract is asserted by the visible test.",
