    "probe_text": "Here is the full ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, read straight from `owners.POST.yml` and the function classes it wires. Every step from `validate` onward runs under one `transaction` governance, so the whole create commits once at the end.\n\n## Before the pipeline\n- **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`): `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 a caller without that role is rejected (403 / `AuthorizationDeniedException`) before any step runs.\n\n## Step 0 \u2014 `checkIdempotency` (`CheckIdempotencyKey`)\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and **publishes it as a variable** (empty when absent).\n- If the key was seen before \u2192 **replay branch**: `LoadStoredOwner` loads the originally-created owner (404 `NotFoundException` if it's gone), then `RespondWithOwner` returns it with **200** (DTO enriched as in the responder below). The create pipeline is skipped entirely.\n- Otherwise (new or keyless) \u2192 proceeds to `validate`.\n\n## Validations (in order) \u2014 `validate` (`ValidateNewOwner`)\nRunning as a single step, in this internal order:\n1. **Normalize the address** \u2014 structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` is preferred when `addressLine1` is non-blank, otherwise the flat `address`; the canonical flat `address` is written back onto the request. *(side-effect on the request DTO)*\n2. **Required-field check** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (tested *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone`; any missing/blank \u2192 **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing the offending names.\n3. **Normalize telephone to E.164** and write it back; a number that can't form valid E.164 \u2192 **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n4. **Normalize email** and write it back; can raise **400** `InvalidEmailException` or `DisposableEmailDomainException` (disposable-domain blocklist).\n5. **Postcode validation** (only when supplied) \u2014 must be a 4-digit code valid for the city's region; malformed/out-of-range \u2192 **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode is accepted.\n6. **Registration-date check** \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date \u2192 **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Absent is accepted (defaulted later).\n7. Publishes the normalized request for later steps.\n\n## Business-rule guards (each can reject; run before anything is built/persisted)\n- `checkIdentityUnique` (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`) \u2014 unless the request declares `sharesHousehold`, computes the `identityKey` (normalized telephone + email + `soundex(lastName)`) and scans all non-soft-deleted owners; an exact match \u2192 **409** `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`.\n- `checkCityCapacity` (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`) \u2014 city already holding **\u2265 50** owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409** `OwnerCityFullException`.\n- `checkDailyLimit` (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`) \u2014 **\u2265 100** owners already carrying the business-day-adjusted effective registration date \u2192 **429** `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n## Side-effects that build the entity (mutations, in order)\n- `build` (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner`; defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent; **rolls it forward to a business day** (weekend \u2192 next Monday). Publishes the `Owner`.\n- `assignMemberId` (`AssignMemberId`) \u2014 computes `memberId` = `<REGION-v2><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, de-duplicating against existing `memberId`s by appending `-<n>` on collision.\n- `assignHousehold` (`AssignHousehold`) \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` from last name + postcode.\n- `assignNamesakeCount` (`AssignNamesakeCount`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), counted before this owner exists.\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (soundex(lastName)+postcode overlap but different identityKey); a declared household member is left unflagged.\n\n## Persistence & post-save side-effects (in order)\n- `save` (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; the generated id becomes available.\n- `audit` (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 emits two `AUDIT` log events: a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON with a sequence number.\n- `welcome` (`EnqueueWelcomeNotification`) \u2014 emits a `NOTIFY` log line (owner id + memberId).\n- `recordIdempotency` (`RecordIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` so future repeats replay; no-op when keyless.\n\n## Response \u2014 `respond` (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`)\n- Maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and enriches it: `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag`, `membershipPoints`, and capped `membershipLevel`.\n- Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nAnything thrown along the way is turned into the HTTP status above by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/`; the transaction spanning `validate`\u2192`respond` commits only if no step escalates."
